  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/... \nDeterministic and ensemble guidance shows the 500 mb ridge axis \nflattening as a weak trough passes through the Intermountain West \nearly next week before rebuilding over SoCal and the Great Basin \nregion again by mid- week. As this pattern evolves, there may be a\nbrief dip in temperatures on Monday before significant warming \noccurs from Tuesday into Thursday. Highs across the western \ndeserts will likely remain in the low 100s Monday and Tuesday \nbefore topping out around 100-105 degrees as early as Wednesday. \nThe lower deserts of southcentral AZ will also see temperatures \ngradually rise from the low to mid 90s Monday and Tuesday to \naround 100 degrees by mid-week. Overnight lows will also be warm, \ngenerally remaining in the low to mid 70s. Overall, daily \ntemperatures are expected peak around 4-8 degrees above normal mid\nto late next week. Subsidence aloft and dry air in the mid lvls \nshould keep a lid on any potential convective, even over the AZ \nhigher terrain and thus rain chances will remain near zero each \nday next week.",
